.\" A man page the corpus's man-tables recording shows, written for the
.\" purpose: tables (tbl), indented lists, examples and every font.
.TH FUX-CORPUS-TABLES 1 2026-10-03 "fux-vt-compare" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fux-corpus-tables \- the engines the corpus is replayed through, in tables
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fux-vt-compare corpus
.RB [ \-\-engines
.IR list ]
.RB [ \-\-show ]
.RI [ name ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Each recording is replayed through
.B fux-vt
and the engines below, and their screens are compared after every step.
.I xterm
decides what it can tell; the panel decides the rest.
.SH ENGINES
.TS
box tab(|);
lb lb lb
l l l.
Engine|Kind|Cannot tell
_
ghostty|in process|link groups
alacritty|in process|blink, 2026, 2048, prompt marks
libvterm|in process|dim, underline colour, kitty
avt|in process|underline colour, hidden, keypad
wezterm|in process|pending wrap, 2026, 2048
vt100|in process|underline colour, blink, hidden
xterm.js|Node|underline colour, kitty, 2048
tmux|a server|kitty, 2026, 2048
xterm|Xvfb|pending wrap, underline colour, kitty
.TE
.SH FIELDS
.TS
allbox tab(:);
cb cb
l lx.
Field:What is compared
text:the whole grapheme cluster of each cell, and its width
style:T{
foreground, background and underline colour; bold, dim, italic,
underline, blink, inverse, hidden and strikeout
T}
link:the URI of an OSC 8 hyperlink, and which cells share it
cursor:its row and column, and whether a wrap is pending
modes:T{
DECAWM, DECOM, DECCKM, DECKPAM, bracketed paste, focus reports,
synchronized output, in-band resize and the kitty keyboard flags
T}
.TE
.SH STATUSES
.IP \(bu 2
.B Agree:
every step agrees beside xterm and the panel.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Differs:
a step differs, for a reason recorded beside it, with the command that
shows it.
.IP \(bu 2
.B New:
a recording with no status, which fails the run until one is given.
.SH EXAMPLES
Replay one recording beside xterm and the panel, and show the screen:
.PP
.EX
$ fux-vt/compare/run.sh corpus \-\-show man-tables
ok       man-tables (9 steps, 6000 bytes)   +xterm +ghostty
.EE
.PP
Record it again:
.PP
.EX
$ fux-vt/compare/corpus/record.sh man-tables
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TS
tab(@);
r l.
0@every recording expected to agree agrees
1@one regressed, or has no status
2@the command line or a recording could not be read
.TE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fux-corpus (1),
.BR fux-corpus-long (7),
.BR less (1)
